# The live season's data folder is written by the sync worker, not by hand.
#
# Tracking it meant every deploy hit "local changes would be overwritten", and
# the usual way out of that - git checkout / reset --hard - silently rewinds
# the two files in here that cannot be re-fetched:
#
#   chat_history.json  the chat archive. The game host keeps fifteen messages
#                      and drops the rest, so anything the archive loses is
#                      gone for good. A reset on 2026-08-30 would have thrown
#                      away four hours of talk.
#   activity.json      when the server was played, built one sample at a time.
#                      There is nothing to rebuild it from.
#
# The rest is re-fetched within a couple of minutes of the worker starting, so
# a fresh clone shows an empty board until the first sync and then fills in.
my_website/static/minecraft/season5/data/
